Package: rcli
Type: Package
Title: Composite Leading and Coincident Indicators from Selection to Validation
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Achmad Syahrul", "Choir", email = "madsyair@stis.ac.id",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
    )
Description: Builds composite leading indicators (CLI) for business and growth
    cycles following the OECD system of composite leading indicators
    (Gyomai and Guidetti 2012). Candidate series are de-trended and smoothed
    (Hodrick and Prescott 1997 <doi:10.2307/2953682>; Christiano and
    Fitzgerald 2003 <doi:10.1111/1468-2354.t01-1-00076>; Hamilton 2018
    <doi:10.1162/rest_a_00706>), turning points are dated with the
    Bry-Boschan and Harding-Pagan rules (Harding and Pagan 2002
    <doi:10.1016/S0304-3932(01)00108-8>), and every candidate is classified
    as leading, coincident, lagging or rejected from its lead at turning
    points, cross-correlation, concordance and Granger causality
    (Toda and Yamamoto 1995 <doi:10.1016/0304-4076(94)01616-8>).
    Leading components are aggregated with equal weights, principal
    components, Conference Board standardisation factors or a dynamic factor
    model, and the composite is re-selected in a loop until it passes
    in-sample and pseudo out-of-sample tests, including a check for the
    selection bias of in-sample leads. A quality scorecard gives an explicit
    verdict on the composite. Coincident components are aggregated the same
    way into a coincident index, tested for timing instead of lead, which can
    replace a quarterly reference series. An optional 'shiny' interface runs
    the workflow step by step. All steps are S4 objects with an audit trail
    of selection decisions.
